  "text": {
    "intro": "Pemberton's holds a blind tasting each spring. The tasters are blind to the tea; the tea is not blind to them.\nFive tasters are involved. Determine each taster's start time, tea and note.\n- **Taster**: Bertrand, Yolanda, Rolf, Marguerite and Chidi.\n- **Start time** (listed from earlier to later): 8am, 9am, 10am, 11am and noon.\n- **Tea**: a Nilgiri frost, a roasted oolong, a smoked Lapsang, a silver needle white and a first-flush Darjeeling.\n- **Tasting note**: stewed apricot; iron filings; wet slate; bruised peach; and hay and honey.\nEvery taster has a different start time, tea and note, so within each category every item is used exactly once.",
    "clues": [
      "The taster who reports bruised peach samples a roasted oolong. The taster who samples a roasted oolong tastes at 8am.",
      "The taster who reports stewed apricot falls somewhere between Marguerite and 9am in start time order. Rolf falls somewhere between 11am and 9am in start time order.",
      "Bertrand and 10am are exactly one hour apart in start time order, in one direction or the other.",
      "The taster who samples a smoked Lapsang is exactly one hour earlier than 10am, with no start time in between.",
      "The taster who samples a Nilgiri frost is exactly one hour earlier than the taster who reports wet slate, with no start time in between.",
      "Rolf and the taster who samples a silver needle white are exactly one hour apart in start time order, in one direction or the other.",
      "Chidi is exactly one hour earlier than the taster who reports stewed apricot, with no start time in between.",
      "The taster who reports hay and honey is earlier than the taster who samples a silver needle white in start time order."
    ]
  }
